WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.866
Numbers arrive one at a time and you must report the median after each.

00:06.866 --> 00:14.700
Re-sorting everything so far after every number does the same work over and over.

00:15.000 --> 00:23.916
Instead, split the numbers into a lower half and an upper half.

00:23.916 --> 00:31.700
Each half only watches the member closest to the split.

00:32.000 --> 00:42.180
15 arrives and lands in the lower half, then the biggest of that half moves across.

00:42.180 --> 00:47.700
Both tops read 5 and 15, so the median is 10.

00:48.000 --> 00:55.597
Each number costs one heap push and pop: O(log n).

00:55.597 --> 00:59.700
That’s the two-heap median.
